# Class: pmd:PMD_0020101 (concentration)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 pmd:PMD_0020101 "Concentrations express the ratio between the quantities of a part and the quantities of the whole.
In contrast to concentrations ratios express the ratio between the quantity of a part and the quantity of the remainder.
To address the (chemical) composition of an enity, see 'composition'."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment pmd:PMD_0020101 "Concentrations can be expressed in terms of three quantifiers:

+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+
|                   | count            | mass              | volume              |
+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+
| per count         | count per count  | (mass per count)  | (volume per count)  |
| per mass          | count per mass   | mass per mass     | volume per mass     |
| per volume        | count per volume | mass per volume   | volume per volume   |
+-------------------+------------------+-------------------+---------------------+

Mass per count and volume per count are not known to have practical examples but are included for completeness."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment pmd:PMD_0020101 "Ratio: 
A comparison of two or more quantities (a relationship), e.g. 3:2:1 for prosecco, aperol and sparkling water in aperol spritz. There is no stanardized mathematical notation or operators for it.  We do not support it, rather convert it to fractions.

Proportion: 
A statement that two ratios/fractions are equal (an equation), e.g. 2/3=4/6"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label pmd:PMD_0020101 "concentration"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition pmd:PMD_0020101 "a property describing a quantitative relation between two entites where one entity represents the whole and the other entity represents a part of the whole"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:example pmd:PMD_0020101 "aperol spritz: 3/6 prosecco, 2/6 aperol, 1/6 sparkling water in vol/vol"@en)
SubClassOf(pmd:PMD_0020101 ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(pmd:PMD_0025999 pmd:PMD_0000001) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(pmd:PMD_0025999 ObjectIntersectionOf(pmd:PMD_0000001 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002350 pmd:PMD_0000001)))))
DisjointUnion(pmd:PMD_0020101 pmd:PMD_0020102 pmd:PMD_0020103 pmd:PMD_0020104 pmd:PMD_0020267 pmd:PMD_0020268 pmd:PMD_0020269 pmd:PMD_0020271 pmd:PMD_0020272 pmd:PMD_0080101)

# Class: pmd:PMD_0020102 (mass fraction)

